<spell-notebook "icon usage">
	<header level="1">
		Icon
		<header>An icon is a glyph used to represent something else.</>
	</>
	<icon-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#using-it">Using it</>
			<item link="#icon-packs">Icon packs</>
			<item link="#keyboard">Keyboard</>
			<item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			`name` is the only thing an icon needs: one name per icon, words separated by spaces (Font Awesome's dashed
			`circle-check` works too). A trailing `outline` names the regular icon; `lucide:bell` asks one pack.

			- Icons also work as the `icon` attribute of other components (`<ui-button icon="download">`), where they share
			  this name resolution.
			- Words go in the icon's own order: `arrow right`, not Fomantic's `right arrow` (a name that isn't in any pack
			  draws nothing).
			- `<ui-icons>` groups icons: the first is the base glyph, the rest stack on it; `corner` puts a small badge on
			  a corner.
			- Icons have no events.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Icon packs">
		<markdown>
			A pack is a folder of SVG files plus a `pack.js` index; the page's packs are shared by every component. Font
			Awesome 7 Free (solid + regular) is the default. Add more for a subtree with `<ui-root icons>`, a
			comma-separated list of built-in ids or `pack.js` URLs (the last pack wins a name; a nested root adds to its
			outer root's packs).
		</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<ui-root icons="fa7-brands">...</ui-root>                      <!-- every brand logo -->
			<ui-root icons="fomantic">...</ui-root>                        <!-- Fomantic's names -->
			<ui-root icons="fa7-free, /icons/lucide/pack.js">...</ui-root> <!-- your own pack, after the default -->
			<ui-root icons="fomantic" assets="/assets/ui/">...</ui-root>   <!-- built-ins load from /assets/ui/icon-packs/ -->
			```
		</>
		<markdown>
			A page without a root adds them from JS: `UI.icons.use("fa7-brands")`, with `{ prefix, base, only }` options.
			Turn any folder of SVGs into a pack with `yarn icons:pack <folder> --id <id>`.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Keyboard">
		<markdown>
			An icon takes no focus and handles no keys, `link` or not: the `<a>` or `<button>` around it does.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- An icon is decorative by default: `aria-hidden="true"` on the host, so screen readers skip it.
			- Give a meaningful icon a `label`: the host becomes `role="img"` with that `aria-label`. Same for a
			  `<ui-icons>` group.
			- An icon that is the only content of a control (`<ui-button icon="cloud">`) needs the name on the control, not
			  the icon.
			- `link` is only the look: wrap the icon in a real `<a>` or `<button>` for interaction.
			- If the icon fails to render, it shows only children written inside it, through a bare `<slot>`: the
			  glyph, its box (size, colour, ring), the `role` and the `label` go.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
